264
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,560
No matter what, I'll always respect him.

265
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:52,157
I believe it's about time for you!

266
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:54,020
To take responsibility.

267
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:56,539
Thoughts, Bellamy?

268
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:59,637
You worship the ground I walked on.

269
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:02,737
But when things got too
tough, you got desperate.

270
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:04,257
Truly pathetic.

271
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:08,557
Cry if you like, but people can't
change the nature they're born with.

272
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:12,940
How sad you'll never amount to
anything more than a dime a dozen thug.

273
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:14,410
Bellamy.

274
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:21,140
Bellamy did change!

275
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:23,400
You take that back now!

276
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,100
It's okay.

277
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:29,200
Kill me already.

278
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:31,680
I beg you.

279
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:36,140
Hey! Straw Hats!

280
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,720
Set Bellamy free!

281
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,470
Mingo!

282
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:46,320
Damn it, I'm sorry!

283
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,717
Didn't we just talk about this, huh?

284
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:49,740
You moron!

285
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:53,960
I told you, if you lose your cool,
he gets exactly what he wants.

286
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:55,460
He's provoking you.

287
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:58,680
Control your anger, or he wins.

288
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:03,337
Next time you lose your temper,
you could wind up losing your head.

289
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:06,480
I foolishly found that out firsthand.

290
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:10,264
Doflamingo is a manipulative,
heartless monster.

291
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:13,586
Always looking to expose
a moment of weakness.

292
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,740
You kicked your dying buddy in the face.

293
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:22,460
Now that's a riot.

294
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:24,920
Why'd you do that?

295
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:31,060
He sure see better days. Bam!

296
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:32,339
Right in the nose.

297
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:36,400
What'd you say?

298
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,211
They're just goading you.

299
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:42,257
How dare you, law!

300
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:45,877
I'm hurt—you think of me as
heartless, spiteful, maybe,

301
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,477
and a man who loses his
temper from time to time?

302
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:51,097
Yes, but heartless—give
me a bit more credit!

303
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:54,377
Think about the position
you all put me in.

304
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:55,817
Remember what you did?

305
00:18:55,900 --> 00:19:00,937
You started this by
destroying my sad production.

306
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,040
sad production

307
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:05,250
machinery.

308
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:07,877
Then you attacked both Vergo and Monet.

309
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:10,037
You also abducted Caesar.

310
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,640
Recently you barged

311
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:15,697
into my home here in Dressrosa
and freed all the toys.

312
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:18,980
And at present, your people are currently

313
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,300
attempting to destroy my smile factory.

314
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:24,777
I tolerated your antics long enough.

315
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:29,397
But you know I am still smiling
because i'm thinking about

316
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:32,697
what i'll do to you what's most
insulting is that you think

317
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:36,277
you can come up and kill me
though i admit you have made my

318
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:42,477
life difficult it feels like i'm
re-experiencing the trauma of

319
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:48,397
what happened 13 years ago if
it wasn't for that moment i

320
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:51,997
would have never come back seeking
revenge on a twisted bastard

321
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:56,937
like you if it wasn't for that
very incident law you'd be here

322
00:19:57,020 --> 00:20:01,520
answering to me as Corazon you
know that's the undeniable truth

323
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:15,200
Now, Black Man gives him a show!

324
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,150
Huh?

325
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:19,280
Another clone?

326
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:27,580
Take that one, Traffy!

327
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:29,680
I'll get the real Mingo!

328
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,000
Move, Bellamy!

329
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,300
Hey, what was that?

330
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:40,737
I thought we were cool!

331
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,640
I told you I was sorry!

332
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,100
Straw Hats, he's being used like a puppet!

333
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:57,900
I'm sorry, Straw Hats!

334
00:20:58,820 --> 00:20:59,880
Stop me!

335
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:09,960
I don't know how important this guy is
to you, but if you want him to stop,

336
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:11,537
you need to knock his lights out!

337
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:12,940
Just listen to him!

338
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,480
Please throw a hat!

339
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,480
I can't do it!

340
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:22,740
Here, my friend!

341
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:40,520
Another hit or two from your
pal should finish you off.

342
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:45,520
Seems like a fitting end for you.

343
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:49,716
You remember what I told you
all those years ago, Law?

344
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:55,080
Weaklings don't have the right
to decide how they get to die.

345
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:02,600
You bastard, Mingo!

346
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:06,780
We came all this way and the
coward won't fight us himself!

347
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:08,580
Hey, Trappy!

348
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,340
I think it's time!

349
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:13,400
He's pissing me off!

350
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,600
You moron!

351
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,460
That's our secret plan!

352
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:20,660
You never listen, do you?

353
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:22,000
I'm calling it!

354
00:22:24,420 --> 00:22:25,780
You dumbass!

355
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,460
I can strangle you!

356
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:32,080
Is he going straight for law?

357
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:34,977
Did his brain go mush
under all this pressure?

358
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:36,500
Now that's too funny!

359
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:40,440
Move! Go!

360
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:47,580
Ready, shambles!

361
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:51,360
Red Hulk! Ah!

362
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:55,290
Ah!

363
00:22:58,100 --> 00:22:58,930
Ah! Ah!

364
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:00,570
Dolphin!

365
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:03,970
Ah!

366
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:06,870
Ah!

367
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:09,370
Ah!

368
00:23:09,453 --> 00:23:10,283
Now, radio knife.

369
00:23:11,180 --> 00:23:12,010
Ah!

370
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:15,300
Damn it, Straw Hatch!

371
00:23:15,460 --> 00:23:17,636
You really are the worst, aren't you?

372
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:19,000
What can I say?

373
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:22,820
That's just our generation.
